(6. Miniature circuit breakers shall conform to IS/IEC 60898-1 and shall have a breaking) Tj T*
(capacity of 10kA.) Tj T*
(7. MCB ratings shall range from 6A to 32A as shown in the single line diagram.) Tj T*
(8. RCCBs with rated residual operating current of 30 mA shall be provided for all socket outlet) Tj T*
(circuits and shall conform to IS 12640 \(Part 1\).) Tj T*
(9. Earthing shall be carried out in accordance with IS 3043:2018.) Tj T*
(10. Two numbers of pipe earth electrodes shall be provided for the main distribution board.) Tj T*
(11. The earth resistance shall not exceed 1 ohms.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6 TESTS AND INSPECTION) Tj T*
(1. Compressive strength tests shall be carried out as per IS 516 \(Part 1/Sec 1\):2021.) Tj T*
(2. Manufacturer's test certificates shall be furnished for each lot of cement and reinforcement) Tj T*
(steel.) Tj T*
(3. Wires shall be tested in accordance with IS 10810.) Tj T*
(4. On completion, insulation resistance and earth continuity tests shall be carried out in) Tj T*
(accordance with IS 732.) Tj T*
(5. Wires, MCBs and RCCBs shall be ISI marked.) Tj T*
(6. The equipment shall be inspected by the Engineer-in-charge at the manufacturer's works) Tj T*
(before dispatch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(1. The contractor shall submit detailed shop drawings for approval within 21 days of award of) Tj T*
(work. Three sets of operation and maintenance manuals shall be handed over on completion.) Tj T*
(2. The complete installation shall be guaranteed against defective design, material and) Tj T*
(workmanship for a period of 12 months from the date of handing over.) Tj T*
(3. The contractor shall train the Department's operating staff in operation and routine) Tj T*
(maintenance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
